  "story": {
    "language": "en",
    "translationLanguage": "zh-Hant",
    "textEn": "In science class, our teacher asks each student to be careful with the water on the table. My friend holds a ruler beside a bottle so we can measure the height of the water. We look at the level of the liquid beside the ruler and tell the teacher what we see. Next, I take some blue water and some yellow water, ready to mix both colors. I add them with care to a glass and watch a new color appear as the water moves together. The result is green, and we keep looking as the color spreads through the water. An empty glass waits beside a full glass, and a cup stays at the end of the table. A drop lands on the table, so we clean it up before moving our things. Our teacher smiles and asks us to explain what changed, using the things we can see.",
    "textZh": "在科學課上，老師請每位學生小心處理桌上的水。朋友把尺拿在瓶子旁，讓我們測量水的高度。我們看看尺旁液體的水位，告訴老師看到什麼。接著，我拿一些藍色水和一些黃色水，準備把兩種顏色混合。我慢慢把它們加入玻璃杯，看著水混在一起，出現新的顏色。結果變成綠色，我們繼續看著顏色在水中散開。一個空玻璃杯放在裝滿水的玻璃杯旁，桌子的另一端還有一個杯子。一滴水落在桌上，所以我們移動物品前先把它擦掉。老師微笑著請我們用看得到的事物，說明發生了什麼變化。",
